WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:05.640
Go for it, go for it

00:08.480 --> 00:09.549
It's all yours for the taking

00:09.550 --> 00:11.949
- It's all yours for the taking -
This is such a great recording.

00:11.950 --> 00:14.139
It's all yours for the taking

00:14.140 --> 00:14.970
Come on!

00:15.690 --> 00:17.539
You're watching the video again?

00:17.540 --> 00:19.629
And look at all this fan mail!

00:19.630 --> 00:21.529
Three pieces.

00:21.530 --> 00:24.289
And isn't one from
Samazu and Namimaru?

00:24.290 --> 00:26.059
They're always
sending you messages.

00:26.060 --> 00:29.460
That's fine. It's different
when it's official snail mail!

00:29.940 --> 00:31.919
That's the "official" method?

00:31.920 --> 00:34.489
I think I'll watch
the video again.

00:34.490 --> 00:45.300
Come on!

00:47.950 --> 00:49.780
She's so entertaining.

02:21.280 --> 02:23.159
SECRET IDENTITY

02:23.160 --> 02:27.079
SECRET IDENTITY THE TRUE PERSON BEHIND THE MASK
OF ANONYMITY WORN BY SPIES, SUPERHEROES, ETC.

02:27.080 --> 02:28.329
SECRET IDENTITY THE TRUE PERSON BEHIND THE MASK OF ANONYMITY
WORN BY SPIES, SUPERHEROES, ETC. WHAT A MAN TAKES WITH HIM

02:28.330 --> 02:29.370
WHAT A MAN TAKES WITH HIM

02:34.800 --> 02:36.069
A mantis villain?!

02:36.070 --> 02:37.380
Run!

02:45.720 --> 02:47.389
That's far enough!

02:47.390 --> 02:51.309
I'm the vigilante who pops up
when someone calls for help!

02:51.310 --> 02:52.890
The Crawler!

02:57.830 --> 03:00.240
Help!

03:01.370 --> 03:04.280
Call for a hero! Now!

03:05.420 --> 03:07.180
One's already been summoned.

03:10.790 --> 03:13.769
Good afternoon,
people of Naruhata.

03:13.770 --> 03:16.799
Captain Celebrity here.

03:16.800 --> 03:17.699
Hell yeah!

03:17.700 --> 03:18.669
Just kidding.

03:18.670 --> 03:20.750
Enough with the intro!

03:22.890 --> 03:24.300
Captain!

03:27.200 --> 03:31.080
You bailed me out.
Thanks as always, Captain.

03:32.120 --> 03:34.309
I'm the one who
should thank you.

03:34.310 --> 03:40.099
It's brave boys like you who're
guarding the peace in this town.

03:40.100 --> 03:44.319
In fact, I'd like to have a chat
with you about ongoing justice.

03:44.320 --> 03:45.609
You got a minute?

03:45.610 --> 03:47.540
Oh, sure.

03:48.010 --> 03:51.120
You know, I'm not
so keen on your style,

03:51.390 --> 03:55.580
the way you prod villains
and then get in over your head.

03:55.980 --> 03:58.160
Well, you have a point.

03:58.570 --> 04:02.679
But it's not like everyone has
special abilities the way heroes do.

04:02.680 --> 04:07.629
We ordinary citizens help each
other to the best of our abilities,

04:07.630 --> 04:11.129
and then get help from pros when
it's something that's beyond us.

04:11.130 --> 04:15.009
Isn't that the way things should
work in a society of Quirks?

04:15.010 --> 04:17.519
You've got the right idea there.

04:17.520 --> 04:21.239
If that's how you think, would you
mind acting like an ordinary citizen?

04:21.240 --> 04:24.570
What you're doing goes
beyond "helping each other."

04:24.940 --> 04:30.489
When you play your silly hero games,
it needlessly adds to my workload.

04:30.490 --> 04:33.809
It's really inconvenient,
to put it bluntly.

04:33.810 --> 04:35.530
I'm sorry.

04:35.860 --> 04:37.139
Hey, Captain.

04:37.140 --> 04:39.879
Could you show up
at the next Narufest?

04:39.880 --> 04:42.549
I don't get paid for that stuff.

04:42.550 --> 04:44.849
And it's hard to
rearrange my schedule.

04:44.850 --> 04:48.629
When you put it that way,
it's not like we get paid either.

04:48.630 --> 04:50.629
We're just busting
our butts after school.

04:50.630 --> 04:53.349
You guys are doing
that stuff for fun.

04:53.350 --> 04:55.749
I'm talking about my job.

04:55.750 --> 04:56.859
Pop.

04:56.860 --> 05:01.059
It'd be faster if you
went straight to Makoto.

05:01.060 --> 05:03.389
He'll just gripe and
give you a hard time.

05:03.390 --> 05:04.830
Oh, yeah.

05:05.070 --> 05:09.249
You two don't have
enough respect for pro work.

05:09.250 --> 05:10.679
Now, now.

05:10.680 --> 05:11.889
On that note,

05:11.890 --> 05:14.910
does someone so concerned about his
schedule have time to slack off at my place?

05:15.280 --> 05:16.509
Hey, listen.

05:16.510 --> 05:19.819
Makoto already keeps
my days packed full as it is.

05:19.820 --> 05:22.290
I don't have any
time for breaks.

05:22.990 --> 05:26.719
I'll at least take a rest here
when you drop me a line.

05:26.720 --> 05:28.429
I'm fully within my rights!

05:28.430 --> 05:32.410
I don't mind if you take a
breather before you go. Just...

05:34.370 --> 05:35.699
Hello.

05:35.700 --> 05:37.370
Oh, Makoto.

05:37.680 --> 05:40.119
Is my boss at your place?

05:40.120 --> 05:41.899
You mean the Captain?

05:41.900 --> 05:43.939
Shh!

05:43.940 --> 05:45.189
He says he's not here.

05:45.190 --> 05:46.079
You!

05:46.080 --> 05:47.369
Oh, really?

05:47.370 --> 05:48.439
- No!
- Huh?

05:48.440 --> 05:49.189
S-Sorry, girl. I need in.

05:49.190 --> 05:50.950
- S-Sorry, girl. I need in.
- I'm getting changed!

05:51.360 --> 05:53.149
I'll sue!

05:53.150 --> 05:56.240
No, don't. I can't
deal with a lawsuit.

05:56.810 --> 05:59.570
Fancy running
into you here, boss.

06:00.820 --> 06:03.739
After I saved the boy, I
brought him back here,

06:03.740 --> 06:06.429
and the enthusiastic
kid insisted I stick around.

06:06.430 --> 06:07.799
I see.

06:07.800 --> 06:09.549
TODAY'S SCHEDULE FOR CAPTAIN CELEBRITY SETUP WITH PHOTOGRAPHY STAFF ON-LOCATION COMMERCIAL
SHOOT - But you've got a commercial shoot, and interviews with a financial magazine

06:09.550 --> 06:10.639
TODAY'S SCHEDULE FOR CAPTAIN CELEBRITY FINANCIAL MAGAZINE INTERVIEW INTERVIEW & PHOTO SHOOT FOR FASHION MAGAZINE
GQQ IN TRANSIT (BREAK) DINNER PARTY - But you've got a commercial shoot, and interviews with a financial magazine

06:10.640 --> 06:13.009
TODAY'S SCHEDULE FOR CAPTAIN CELEBRITY FINANCIAL MAGAZINE INTERVIEW INTERVIEW & PHOTO SHOOT FOR FASHION
MAGAZINE GQQ IN TRANSIT (BREAK) DINNER PARTY - and a fashion magazine lined up, so let's get a move on.

06:13.010 --> 06:13.020
and a fashion magazine
lined up, so let's get a move on.

06:13.280 --> 06:14.280
Up we go!

06:16.040 --> 06:17.419
And they're gone.

06:17.420 --> 06:19.830
They sure do keep busy.

06:20.940 --> 06:26.159
Well, it is true that we cause trouble
for the Captain and the other heroes.

06:26.160 --> 06:30.110
Maybe we should stay away
from villains who look too strong?

06:30.650 --> 06:31.910
Or more like...

06:32.580 --> 06:36.930
It seems lately, there've
been a lot of strong villains.

06:37.640 --> 06:41.740
Or like, it's different from the
Trigger effects we had been seeing.

06:42.260 --> 06:44.129
Some of them are
overly ferocious,

06:44.130 --> 06:46.789
or they don't transform
back even when unconscious.

06:46.790 --> 06:50.770
Does that means they're genuine
villains? No drugs involved?

06:51.390 --> 06:53.789
Hmm, I'm not sure.

06:53.790 --> 06:56.220
It's hard to tell with
Master not around.

06:57.010 --> 07:00.399
Maybe I should carry some
kind of weapons with me too.

07:00.400 --> 07:02.889
For self-defense, I guess.

07:02.890 --> 07:03.929
Really?

07:03.930 --> 07:07.749
You were saying that sort of
thing before, too, about a sword.

07:07.750 --> 07:11.329
If you actually went and did
that, I don't think it would end well.

07:11.330 --> 07:14.409
There's nothing that says
you have to go fight villains.

07:14.410 --> 07:16.609
You could be more
of a freelance sidekick.

07:16.610 --> 07:20.739
Just stick to finding people in
trouble and calling a hero for them.

07:20.740 --> 07:22.520
Got to know your place.

07:24.920 --> 07:26.619
Maybe you're right.

07:26.620 --> 07:27.900
Sure I am.

07:29.460 --> 07:31.849
A new type of villain?

07:31.850 --> 07:37.270
Yes. Perhaps you'd call it a
new variant of instant villain.

07:37.570 --> 07:40.519
Take Teruo
Unagisawa, for instance.

07:40.520 --> 07:43.149
Unlike with his first offense,
when we arrested him again,

07:43.150 --> 07:45.859
there'd been a big shift in his
size and physical characteristics.

07:45.860 --> 07:46.789
QUIRK: ELECTRIC EEL - there'd been a big shift
in his size and physical characteristics.

07:46.790 --> 07:47.129
there'd been a big shift in his
size and physical characteristics.

07:47.130 --> 07:50.429
He doesn't even look
like the same person.

07:50.430 --> 07:53.909
Upon examination, a doctor said it
wasn't due to an out-of-control Quirk,

07:53.910 --> 07:56.319
but rather, it's a
semipermanent modification.

07:56.320 --> 08:00.909
Including him, we've detected
something in the blood of the villains

08:00.910 --> 08:05.379
who've been arrested lately in
the Naruhata area: Ideo Trigger

08:05.380 --> 08:08.169
at concentrations well above
what's normally a lethal dose.

08:08.170 --> 08:12.879
You're saying their bodies
changed due to a Trigger overdose?

08:12.880 --> 08:16.480
No, we think it's the opposite.

08:16.770 --> 08:21.930
We suspect someone has
artificially given them the ability

08:22.330 --> 08:25.399
to withstand Trigger overdoses.

08:25.400 --> 08:28.950
In that case, this is
clearly organized crime.

08:29.260 --> 08:33.400
Then what might be this
organization's goal, I wonder.

08:33.920 --> 08:36.779
An instant villain whose
reason has gone out the window

08:36.780 --> 08:40.330
isn't capable of carrying out
an intricately planned crime.

08:40.650 --> 08:42.249
When it comes to this new type,

08:42.250 --> 08:45.490
they can't even run and hide
once their rampage is over.

08:45.840 --> 08:49.740
For all their flashiness, they're
ultimately just disposable pawns.

08:50.410 --> 08:53.539
Which means there's someone
scheming behind the scenes,

08:53.540 --> 08:55.900
all while sacrificing pieces.

08:56.510 --> 08:56.879
MARUKANE

08:56.880 --> 08:58.719
MARUKANE - Ladies and gentlemen!

08:58.720 --> 09:01.220
Thank you for your
ongoing support!

09:01.510 --> 09:06.799
This is Narufest, your free community
show hosted by Marukane Department Store!

09:06.800 --> 09:08.399
Our final morning-block
song is Can't Help Loving You

09:08.400 --> 09:10.589
POP LOVE - Our final morning-block
song is Can't Help Loving You

09:10.590 --> 09:11.109
POP LOVE - by The Little Sisters,
from Saint Lila's Academy for Girls!

09:11.110 --> 09:15.210
by The Little Sisters, from
Saint Lila's Academy for Girls!

09:15.730 --> 09:16.820
Take it away!

09:17.760 --> 09:18.939
Ready, go!

09:18.940 --> 09:23.040
Love, love, love, love you lots

09:24.290 --> 09:26.170
We never stop moving forward.

09:26.410 --> 09:29.310
So long as we have the
drive to break through,

09:31.550 --> 09:35.250
this loop will once
again lead into the future.

09:36.720 --> 09:42.130
The Naruhata section of the Capital Central
Loop Highway has been fully restored!

09:42.560 --> 09:47.730
Okay! Let's stop here, then overlay
a caption! The timing's perfect!

09:48.240 --> 09:50.209
That should do nicely.

09:50.210 --> 09:54.730
Hmm. Could you back
that up a few frames?

09:56.990 --> 10:02.250
See, right before the freeze,
some of my hair is down in my face.

10:02.600 --> 10:04.749
Not a good look, is it?

10:04.750 --> 10:07.580
Well, it's only
onscreen for a moment,

10:07.970 --> 10:10.049
and we can CG
it out if you like.

10:10.050 --> 10:13.299
Doing a retake would
also ask a lot of Ingenium.

10:13.300 --> 10:15.989
Nah, my legs can handle another.

10:15.990 --> 10:18.460
We're here, we might as
well shoot one more take.

10:18.760 --> 10:21.639
Sorry he's so
demanding, Ingenium.

10:21.640 --> 10:24.419
Not at all, he's an
international hero.

10:24.420 --> 10:25.970
He doesn't
compromise on the job.

10:26.370 --> 10:28.680
You're a pro too.
And a lifesaver!

10:29.770 --> 10:33.000
Yes. A lifesaver, indeed.

10:33.900 --> 10:35.139
MEETING ROOM B GREEN ROOM
POP FEATHERS THE LITTLE SISTERS

10:35.140 --> 10:36.150
MEETING ROOM B GREEN ROOM POP
FEATHERS THE LITTLE SISTERS - Listen up.

10:36.490 --> 10:39.959
This is your first time, so you
girls might not quite realize,

10:39.960 --> 10:44.819
but Narufest is more than just
your run-of-the-mill amateur event.

10:44.820 --> 10:48.470
Famous pro heroes show up,
and we take our stagecraft seriously.

10:50.960 --> 10:52.199
Yes, ma'am!

10:52.200 --> 10:53.500
Good.

10:54.000 --> 10:54.269
MEETING ROOM B GREEN ROOM
POP FEATHERS THE LITTLE SISTERS

10:54.270 --> 10:55.709
MEETING ROOM B GREEN ROOM POP
FEATHERS THE LITTLE SISTERS - What?!

10:55.710 --> 10:55.719
What?!

10:55.720 --> 10:57.699
The Captain's not coming?!

10:57.700 --> 11:01.929
I tried asking Makoto, but she said
he's shooting a commercial today.

11:01.930 --> 11:05.259
Oh great, I just made
an empty promise!

11:05.260 --> 11:06.640
Yeah, I saw.

11:09.480 --> 11:13.970
Um, may I ask which
hero will be here?

11:14.560 --> 11:17.429
I-It's a secret!
Because it's a surprise!

11:17.430 --> 11:18.199
Miu!

11:18.200 --> 11:20.660
Hi! How's everyone doing?

11:21.160 --> 11:23.070
Oh, Koichi.

11:25.720 --> 11:27.829
Can I have a green room lunch?

11:27.830 --> 11:29.600
There's one extra, right?

11:30.270 --> 11:31.780
Miu, you wouldn't!

11:32.370 --> 11:34.839
So, the intermission is over.

11:34.840 --> 11:38.549
I'd like to introduce
today's special guest.

11:38.550 --> 11:44.219
He's Naruhata's own like-a-hero
but not, kinda hero-ish guy!

11:44.220 --> 11:46.220
The Crawler!

11:53.420 --> 11:54.800
Don't look at me!

11:55.330 --> 11:56.390
Do something!

11:57.960 --> 11:59.740
Um...

12:00.210 --> 12:03.559
Well, since I'm up
here, I'll sing a song.

12:03.560 --> 12:06.949
It's Can't Help Loving
You, by Otomezaka 55.

12:06.950 --> 12:07.829
That song?!

12:07.830 --> 12:09.450
It just got sung!

12:09.790 --> 12:14.070
Love, love, love, love you lots

12:14.720 --> 12:16.280
I can't help it!

12:16.870 --> 12:17.920
Whoo!

12:18.220 --> 12:19.249
In this moment I dreamed of

12:19.250 --> 12:22.369
- In this moment I dreamed of - And he
doesn't completely suck, which makes it worse.

12:22.370 --> 12:24.019
- I hold your hand and
think back - We're so sorry!

12:24.020 --> 12:26.109
- I hold your hand and think back
- No problem, that guy is a trip.

12:26.110 --> 12:26.799
- A casual gesture - No
problem, that guy is a trip.

12:26.800 --> 12:28.149
- A casual gesture
- This is fun!

12:28.150 --> 12:28.599
A casual gesture

12:28.600 --> 12:30.079
By the way, when do
we get to meet the hero?

12:30.080 --> 12:31.889
- Makes my heart tremble - By the
way, when do we get to meet the hero?

12:31.890 --> 12:33.809
- Makes my heart tremble - Oh
no, this didn't solve the problem.

12:33.810 --> 12:34.099
Oh no, this didn't
solve the problem.

12:34.100 --> 12:35.339
- I want to treasure - Oh no,
this didn't solve the problem.

12:35.340 --> 12:35.800
I want to treasure

12:36.570 --> 12:38.269
Everyone ready on the set!

12:38.270 --> 12:40.990
Scene 21, take 3!

12:41.570 --> 12:42.710
Roll camera!

12:46.620 --> 12:47.660
Ready!

12:48.590 --> 12:49.500
Action!

13:02.010 --> 13:03.290
Boss!

13:06.010 --> 13:08.430
Ingenium! Villain
closing on your six!

13:08.950 --> 13:10.050
I see him!

13:11.500 --> 13:12.520
He's big.

13:13.640 --> 13:14.850
And fast!

13:17.220 --> 13:20.560
That visor... Is he that
same bat creep from before?

13:21.830 --> 13:22.810
You won't escape!

13:23.280 --> 13:27.980
I-Ingenium... Just give up.

13:29.480 --> 13:31.139
You lose.

13:31.140 --> 13:32.840
Fall to your death!

13:33.750 --> 13:37.710
Those two... are next.

13:45.830 --> 13:46.880
Hey!

13:47.210 --> 13:48.300
Ingenium!

13:48.530 --> 13:51.019
I'm fine! Please
chase down that villain!

13:51.020 --> 13:52.220
Will do!

13:54.690 --> 13:58.429
Looks like he's got me
matched in speed, at least.

13:58.430 --> 14:00.429
I won't catch up at this rate!

14:00.430 --> 14:02.850
C.C., please maintain pursuit.

14:05.020 --> 14:08.219
We'll request help from heroes in
the metro area to surround the villain.

14:08.220 --> 14:11.459
Aw, wouldn't that make
me look incompetent?

14:11.460 --> 14:14.209
Makoto! The boss
is griping again!

14:14.210 --> 14:15.080
Boss!

14:15.850 --> 14:18.499
I-I hear him.

14:18.500 --> 14:22.209
Our love speeds up
every time we meet

14:22.210 --> 14:26.289
- I see the future behind your
eyes - I've caught his scent!

14:26.290 --> 14:28.749
The Crawler!

14:28.750 --> 14:30.519
...waiting for us

14:30.520 --> 14:34.309
It goes on and on forever

14:34.310 --> 14:38.160
When we meet, love takes root

14:40.390 --> 14:42.139
A villain came out of the sky!

14:42.140 --> 14:44.029
He flew off with somebody!

14:44.030 --> 14:46.280
K-Koichi!

14:47.940 --> 14:53.750
He is... Captain Celebrity!

14:55.630 --> 14:59.250
Gotcha! Shouldn't have
slowed down, bat guy!

15:07.620 --> 15:10.049
You made for great bait, boy.

15:10.050 --> 15:12.460
You do come in handy sometimes.

15:13.900 --> 15:15.729
Celebrity does it again!

15:15.730 --> 15:17.889
Chris!

15:17.890 --> 15:18.359
You're wonderful!

15:18.360 --> 15:19.389
- You're wonderful!
- Hi there, folks!

15:19.390 --> 15:19.969
Hi there, folks!

15:19.970 --> 15:21.439
Big Bro!

15:21.440 --> 15:23.659
Lookin' super good!

15:23.660 --> 15:27.030
Wow, heroes are amazing!

15:27.300 --> 15:29.690
We wanted to meet you!

15:32.610 --> 15:34.620
Good job, Koichi!

15:41.920 --> 15:43.960
Huh? Those are...

15:45.430 --> 15:48.009
They're what Master
always wears on his hands.

15:48.010 --> 15:49.969
This cloth is his mask.

15:49.970 --> 15:51.839
Did he forget to take them?

15:51.840 --> 15:55.060
I guess he went off to that
NPO-whatever job of his?

15:55.910 --> 15:59.510
Not that I'm sure the
company even exists.

16:00.670 --> 16:03.719
Why would he leave
something behind here, anyway?

16:03.720 --> 16:08.299
I don't know, maybe he came
by specifically to leave them here?

16:08.300 --> 16:10.939
I'm not sure what the point
of that would be, either.

16:10.940 --> 16:14.430
Hmm. Maybe what
he's getting at is...

16:15.610 --> 16:19.149
he wants these washed.
They are kinda dirty.

16:19.150 --> 16:21.540
Or maybe they need maintenance.

16:31.350 --> 16:34.760
Looks like they
haven't used the drug.

16:35.100 --> 16:39.799
Master, there haven't been any
Trigger-related incidents at all lately.

16:39.800 --> 16:43.010
You know how it goes,
though. It could pop up again.

16:43.310 --> 16:45.659
Those types die hard, after all.

16:45.660 --> 16:47.979
Hello, is this the police?

16:47.980 --> 16:51.849
Master, care to take a break at
my place once we're done here?

16:51.850 --> 16:54.109
I've got something
I have to see to.

16:54.110 --> 16:55.649
Could I leave the rest to you?

16:55.650 --> 16:58.240
Okay, I don't mind.

16:59.580 --> 17:00.860
I appreciate it.

17:05.470 --> 17:07.369
Hi, Koichi.

17:07.370 --> 17:09.090
Oh, Makoto.

17:10.110 --> 17:11.549
Oh, isn't that...

17:11.550 --> 17:13.939
Yes, Master's pounder.

17:13.940 --> 17:15.540
"Pounder," eh?

17:15.780 --> 17:19.269
You know, it's high time I got an
interview with that master of yours.

17:19.270 --> 17:22.229
Oh, I don't think
he'll stop by today.

17:22.230 --> 17:23.979
I'll let him know
once I see him.

17:23.980 --> 17:26.769
We never seem to be
here at the same time.

17:26.770 --> 17:28.520
By the way, where's Pop?

17:29.760 --> 17:31.029
Inside. Go ahead.

17:31.030 --> 17:32.030
Thanks.

17:33.880 --> 17:35.690
Hello there!

17:36.140 --> 17:39.069
We received another fan letter!

17:39.070 --> 17:41.279
And here are some
performance photos.

17:41.280 --> 17:42.669
Yay!

17:42.670 --> 17:44.630
The videos are getting
lots of views, too.

17:45.160 --> 17:47.579
And I hear people are telling
Marukane they missed the show,

17:47.580 --> 17:49.709
or they want us to
hold more of them.

17:49.710 --> 17:51.619
Sure thing! I'll do more!

17:51.620 --> 17:53.970
Talk about winning her over.

18:23.490 --> 18:24.510
Who're you?

18:29.600 --> 18:31.110
You look scary.

18:32.410 --> 18:35.340
My hand... won't move.

18:36.890 --> 18:39.520
Head hurts.

18:43.080 --> 18:45.760
Where's... my dad?

18:51.870 --> 18:52.930
Hey.

18:53.250 --> 18:54.680
You're awake, Tamao?

18:56.070 --> 18:57.000
Thanks a lot.

19:02.770 --> 19:04.250
I'll be in touch.

19:05.250 --> 19:07.009
How do you feel?

19:07.010 --> 19:10.430
Probably not bad, since
there's painkillers in your IV.

19:10.890 --> 19:12.430
Want to try eating something?

19:13.560 --> 19:14.950
My head hurts.

19:15.340 --> 19:19.059
Yeah, not much we can
do about the headache.

19:19.060 --> 19:20.330
That's gonna take time.

19:21.580 --> 19:26.050
Well, the best medicine for
you right now is more sleep.

19:28.050 --> 19:29.590
Where's Mom?

19:32.750 --> 19:36.260
You... just missed your mom.

19:36.770 --> 19:38.040
Can't see her right now.

19:59.950 --> 20:03.480
But she was happy
that you'd come home.

20:06.330 --> 20:09.280
Bringing you back
was so worth it.

20:11.900 --> 20:13.280
I can't see her?

20:14.600 --> 20:15.950
For now.

20:17.430 --> 20:19.530
But it's okay, Tamao.

20:20.240 --> 20:21.680
No need to worry.

20:24.240 --> 20:25.600
I'm here.

20:28.450 --> 20:30.339
Hey, Koichi!

20:30.340 --> 20:32.239
Open the door!

20:32.240 --> 20:33.750
What's happening?

20:34.240 --> 20:35.810
Whoa! What's that?

20:36.620 --> 20:41.719
A corkboard? Isn't it a little
big for a home bulletin board?

20:41.720 --> 20:45.329
I'm going to fill it with stuff
like concert pics and fan letters!

20:45.330 --> 20:47.690
Oh, that does sound good.

20:48.340 --> 20:50.779
And I'll hang
Master's things here.

20:50.780 --> 20:53.519
That's not the
point of this board.

20:53.520 --> 20:55.669
And the recycling schedule.

20:55.670 --> 20:57.230
What'd I just say?!

20:57.780 --> 21:00.400
Hello. Is your master in today?

21:01.070 --> 21:03.860
Human memory isn't reliable.

21:04.560 --> 21:08.380
When it comes to Master, I had this image
of him being the head of my household.

21:08.690 --> 21:11.369
But when I take
a good look back,

21:11.370 --> 21:16.340
he was only staying here
for those first few months.

21:17.140 --> 21:20.359
That means my activities
thereafter as The Crawler

21:20.360 --> 21:23.839
were something I did
on my own, without him,

21:23.840 --> 21:26.790
but the fact that it kinda
felt like he was still there

21:27.210 --> 21:30.680
must have everything to do
with his strong sense of presence.

21:31.440 --> 21:36.769
Anyway, my own battle still
hadn't even begun at that point.

21:36.770 --> 21:39.390
Nobody even realized that.

21:40.320 --> 21:44.190
But whether people
realize it or not,

21:44.560 --> 21:46.500
the hands of the
clock keep moving,

21:47.200 --> 21:51.130
and the seasons
slowly come and go.
